    "result_text": "The full build and test suite are green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe owner `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 a deterministic region-and-hash identity with no sequence numbers.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** (rewritten) \u2014 builds `customerCode` as:\n- **REGION**: derived purely from the postcode (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099, else `UNKNOWN`).\n- **HASH8**: first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where the telephone is normalized to E.164 via the existing `TelephoneNormalizer`.\n- No longer touches `OwnerRepository` (the per-city sequence count is gone).\n\n**`LocalityLookup.postcodeRegion(...)`** (new public method) \u2014 exposes the postcode\u2192region derivation (returning `UNKNOWN` when unresolvable), reused by the customer code.\n\nEverything downstream now follows the new identity:\n- **Membership number** (`AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`) \u2014 already `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it inherits the new code unchanged.\n- **Check digit** (`OwnerMapper.checkDigit`) \u2014 Luhn over the digits in the (now hex) customer code, inherits automatically.\n- **Audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 logs the new customer code (verified in run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n- **Locality** (`OwnerMapper.locality`, new) \u2014 now taken from the REGION component of the customer code instead of an independent city/postcode lookup, with a fallback to the old lookup only for owners that have no customer code yet (e.g. seed data).\n\nStale docstrings/comments referencing the old `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN` format and the per-city counting were updated.\n\n## Tests\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserts the `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` shape) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
